  </revision>
  <revision rev="8" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>b5cd1a6f8f83d918486d4bf3f9a50cef</srcmd5>
    <version>1.18.26</version>
    <time>1788361383</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update to opencode 1.18.26.

Upstream bugfix release. The vendored npm closure was retraced: 512 to
507 store entries, SPDX set unchanged over 506 packages and still free
of copyleft (README.SUSE-maint carries the audit). The bun and
@opentui/core pins did not move, so nothing else has to be bumped
alongside. Dropping seroval 1.3.2 with the solid-js/web import also
takes six seroval CVEs out of the bundled binary - incidental, not an
upstream security fix.

Built and %check'd natively on aarch64; OBS x86_64 verified green.</comment>
    <requestid>1375302</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="9" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>bfe99bdfd17d5d8fccdb33d086e88cc7</srcmd5>
    <version>1.18.27</version>
    <time>1788518427</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>opencode 1.18.27.

Upstream: provider header and streamed-chunk timeouts now default to five
minutes (both take false to disable); Anthropic thinking-block binding is
narrowed to Claude 5.1+ and honours a blockBinding: false opt-out; the
rejection from cancelling a timed-out SSE read is caught instead of going
unhandled.

Packaging: vendor keep list retraced, 507 -&gt; 509 store entries but the same
506 packages - ai-gateway-provider 3.2.0 and gitlab-ai-provider 6.12.1 each
get one store entry per @ai-sdk/provider-utils peer resolution (4.0.23 and
4.0.50). SPDX set unchanged, still no copyleft; README.SUSE-maint records the
re-audit. All four patches apply unchanged; the @opentui/core pin stays 0.4.5.

Built locally on aarch64, %check green, rpmlint 0 errors / 0 badness.</comment>
    <requestid>1375573</requestid>
  </revision>
